{"id":"d0b80e288167b306","group":"58","path":"58/batch03/58-lem-fodor.md","title":"Fodor's Lemma","display":"lem-fodor — Fodor's Lemma","type":"lemma","metadata":{"type":"lemma","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-lem-fodor","aliases":["58-lem-fodor","Fodor's Lemma"],"display":"lem-fodor — Fodor's Lemma","depends_on":["[[../batch19/58-df-stationary.md]]","[[../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"lemma"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-lem-fodor"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-lem-fodor</span><span>Fodor's Lemma</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"lem-fodor — Fodor's Lemma"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md\">../batch19/58-df-stationary.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" href=\"?note=aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md\">../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\\in V\">\\(\\kappa\\in V\\)</span> (candidate uncountable regular cardinal)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\\subseteq\\kappa\">\\(S\\subseteq\\kappa\\)</span> (stationary-set candidate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md\">../batch19/58-df-stationary.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"f\\in V\">\\(f\\in V\\)</span> (regressive-function candidate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" href=\"?note=aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md\">../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Stationary},\\mathrm{Regressive}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{Stationary},\\mathrm{Regressive}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (stationarity and regressiveness predicates)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\omega\\in\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists\\xi\\in\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\alpha\\in S:f(\\alpha)=\\xi\\},\\kappa)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\omega\\in\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists\\xi\\in\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\alpha\\in S:f(\\alpha)=\\xi\\},\\kappa)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Fodor (1952): proved the lemma for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa = \\omega_1\">\\(\\kappa = \\omega_1\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The lemma states that a regressive function on a stationary set is constant on a stationary subset.</li>\n<li>Key application: proving properties of stationary sets.</li>\n<li>The stationarity predicate already supplies regular-cardinality and subset guards; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\omega\\in\\kappa\">\\(\\omega\\in\\kappa\\)</span> adds uncountability.</li>\n<li>The conclusion uses a set-bounded value <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\xi\\in\\kappa\">\\(\\xi\\in\\kappa\\)</span>; regressiveness guarantees every value on a nonzero point of <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\">\\(S\\)</span> lies below that same regular cardinal.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch19/58-df-stationary.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch19/58-df-stationary.md","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$S\\subseteq\\kappa$ (stationary-set candidate, see [[../batch19/58-df-stationary.md]])","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md","status":"resolved","id":"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$f\\in V$ (regressive-function candidate, see [[../batch12/58-df-regressive-function.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\kappa\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"S\\subseteq\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"f\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Stationary},\\mathrm{Regressive}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{lem\\text{-}fodor} \\vdash \\omega\\in\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists\\xi\\in\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\alpha\\in S:f(\\alpha)=\\xi\\},\\kappa)","display":true},{"tex":"\\kappa = \\omega_1","display":false},{"tex":"\\omega\\in\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"\\xi\\in\\kappa","display":false},{"tex":"S","display":false}],"bytes":1406,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-3897","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-lem-fodor.md|58-lem-fodor]]（batch03）"}],"outgoing":["b802c3dd76418d95","aa5065a1f0bd9a7f"]}